<title>SPAIN: Telefonica 9-month profit up 19.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Telefonica 9-month profit up 19.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for Spain's Telefonica group for the nine months to September in billions of pesetas, unless stated:</p>
<p> Net attributable profit	   120.23     vs   100.39</p>
<p> Pretax profit			 210.89     vs   169.47</p>
<p> Net taxed			     162.89     vs   138.81</p>
<p> Operating result		    413.99     vs   382.87</p>
<p> Operating income		   1,475.87    vs  1,302.86</p>
<p> Operating costs			746.61    vs    624.25</p>
<p> Depreciation			   392.98    vs    373.28</p>
<p> Financial results		   (123.58)   vs   (153.46)</p>
<p> Earnings per share (pesetas)     127.97    vs    106.85</p>
<p> Cash flow per share (pesetas)    635.29    vs    593.57</p>
<p> Short term debt		     847.05    vs    769.24</p>
<p> Provisions			    323.12    vs    271.04</p>
<p> Shareholders' funds	     1,639.49    vs  1,554.83</p>
<p> Total assets			4,968.59    vs  4,746.28</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name Telefonica de Espana S.A.. The firm said financial expenses fell 15.4 percent in the period on the back of a 2.7 percent decrease in debt and lower interest rates.</p>
</text>
